{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PkhrsJmtpu1HgRrNCRgque","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"88686e67-15f6-420e-923b-5a5a834e5552","uuid":"52c89ddd-9937-46d2-a7e5-df398a3db6dd","timestamp":"2026-06-10T08:17:43.210Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md","oldString":"- **E1 scope:**","newString":"- **sos_57 mana spent:** \"amount of mana spent\" recorded at cast as\n  `card.mana_spent = effective_cost.cmc` (post-reduction mana value) in\n  `cast_spell`. X is treated as 0 (not tracked). Free casts leave it unset\n  (default 0).\n- **sos_57 Wizard timing:** the \"if you control a Wizard\" condition is checked\n  when the delayed ability fires at the next main phase (per TODO), not at Mana\n  Sculpt's resolution. Ambiguous in the oracle; followed the TODO.\n- **sos_57 \"next main phase\":** delayed mana fires at the controller's next\n  precombat main (E2), gated by `turn_number > cast_turn`. Limitation: a\n  same-turn postcombat main isn't covered by E2 (only precombat mains fire it).\n\n- **E1 scope:**","originalFile":"# KEY_DECISIONS.md — SOS card implementation log\n\nOne short entry per ambiguity, deviation from TODO.md, or deliberate\ncard-local limitation. Source of truth is `card_spec.json` + `RULEBOOK.txt`.\n\n- **sos_1 exile-instead:** TODO suggested a `ReplacementEffect` for \"if that\n  spell would be put into your graveyard, exile it instead\", but the engine\n  never consults replacements for stack→graveyard spell resolution. Smallest\n  correct change: a `_exile_on_resolve` flag read at the one right point in\n  `engine.casting._resolve_spell`. Limitation: only redirects on resolution,\n  not on countering (covers the cards in this set).\n- **sos_1 attack trigger / engine:** `AttacksTriggeredEvent` was defined and\n  registered by many FDN cards but never fired by combat. Added a minimal\n  additive firing in `engine.combat.declare_attackers_step` after attackers are\n  declared (fires `creature=attacker`). Justified by sos_1's attack trigger;\n  also fixes Etali et al.\n- **sos_1 \"may cast target\":** single legal graveyard target auto-selects (per\n  TODO); multiple → `choose_card` picks one or returns None to decline.\n\n- **sos_257 restricted mana:** Added `add_restricted` + `_restricted` tracking\n  to `engine.mana.ManaPool`, and a keyword-only `restricted_ok` to\n  `can_pay`/`pay` (default False, backward compatible). `cast_spell` passes\n  `restricted_ok=True` only for instant/sorcery. Unrestricted mana is spent\n  first so restricted mana is preserved.\n- **sos_257 animation:** Land becomes a creature by in-place mutation (add\n  CREATURE type + update `_original_card_types` so cleanup's\n  `_reset_characteristics` preserves it; add Wizard subtype; set creature\n  scaffolding). P/T are properties that raise AttributeError until animated, so\n  SBA/combat `hasattr` guards skip the un-animated land (SBA zero-toughness has\n  no creature-type guard).\n- **sos_257 pump:** \"+1/+0 until end of turn\" is a direct `_pump` counter (the\n  layer system only recomputes at cleanup, too late for mid-turn combat). Reset\n  at upkeep (`BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent`), since no end-of-turn event is\n  fired. Limitation: pump lingers between a turn's cleanup and the next upkeep,\n  unobservable in practice.\n- **Ability activation in tests:** activated/loyalty/mana abilities are not\n  auto-wired into the priority loop, so tests fetch the ability by printed index\n  from the card's `get_*_abilities()` hook and drive it through the engine's\n  `activate_ability` (the real activation path) — not by calling effects\n  directly.\n\n- **E1 scope:** `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` is fired only from `cast_spell`\n  (normal casts), not from `cast_spell_free` or `copy_spell`, per the TODO.\n  Consequence: free casts (Etali-style) and spell copies do not fire \"you\n  cast a spell\" triggers. Deliberate, matches the plan's note that copies are\n  not \"cast\". Populated `spell` (the StackObject), `card`, `controller`, and\n  `player` (alias) for FDN-compat condition readers.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":39,"oldLines":6,"newStart":39,"newLines":17,"lines":["   `activate_ability` (the real activation path) — not by calling effects","   directly."," ","+- **sos_57 mana spent:** \"amount of mana spent\" recorded at cast as","+  `card.mana_spent = effective_cost.cmc` (post-reduction mana value) in","+  `cast_spell`. X is treated as 0 (not tracked). Free casts leave it unset","+  (default 0).","+- **sos_57 Wizard timing:** the \"if you control a Wizard\" condition is checked","+  when the delayed ability fires at the next main phase (per TODO), not at Mana","+  Sculpt's resolution. Ambiguous in the oracle; followed the TODO.","+- **sos_57 \"next main phase\":** delayed mana fires at the controller's next","+  precombat main (E2), gated by `turn_number > cast_turn`. Limitation: a","+  same-turn postcombat main isn't covered by E2 (only precombat mains fire it).","+"," - **E1 scope:** `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` is fired only from `cast_spell`","   (normal casts), not from `cast_spell_free` or `copy_spell`, per the TODO.","   Consequence: free casts (Etali-style) and spell copies do not fire \"you"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
